  "scientific_summary": "Lean address-space diagnostic SUPPORTED under the rule fixed in advance; root recomputed it from receipts. Eight of ten previously kernel-blocked modules failed at the 6 GiB address-space cap with resource signatures and passed at 32 GiB with identical source and olean hashes; two passed at both, consistent with sampled VmPeak of about 6.0 to 6.5 GiB sitting right at the old cap. All ten pass at 32 GiB under the unchanged 6 GiB real-memory guard, 115 s CPU and 130 s deadline. A probe importing Complex, Polynomial, Ideal quotients and Real compiled and kernel-checked at under 2 GiB real memory. A probe with import Mathlib was killed by the unchanged 6 GiB real-memory guard, so formal lanes must use specific imports. The three source-only modules fail with ordinary elaboration errors, not resource errors. Infrastructure evidence only: no module becomes green for any candidate, credit 0, 57/80.",
